<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>XFA Forms on KevCaz's Website</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/xfa-forms/</link><description>Recent content in XFA Forms on KevCaz's Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Content under CC0 1.0 Universal unless otherwise specified.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 25 Mar 2020 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/xfa-forms/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fill out your XFA forms with Master PDF</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/03/2020-03-25_fill_out_your/</link><pubDate>Wed, 25 Mar 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/03/2020-03-25_fill_out_your/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The other day I needed to fill out some &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XFA"&gt;XFA forms&lt;/a&gt;.
On the website I was told to use Acrobat Reader &amp;#x1f628;&amp;hellip; which is &lt;a href="https://unix.stackexchange.com/questions/3505/how-to-install-adobe-acrobat-reader-in-debian"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; supported on Linux&lt;/a&gt;.
So I looked for an alternative to work on Debian 10, when I stumbled into this
&lt;a href="https://askubuntu.com/questions/1184128/is-there-any-software-that-can-fill-xfa-forms-in-ubuntu"&gt;answer on &lt;i class="fab fa-stack-exchange"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
mentioning &lt;a href="https://code-industry.net/free-pdf-editor/"&gt;Master PDF&lt;/a&gt;, so I installed it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ apt-get install master-pdf-editor
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;and you know what? Worked like a charm! &amp;#x1f386;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>